# Not site content: read by wrangler or git, never uploaded as an asset.
# Neither directory is skipped by wrangler on its own (measured, wrangler
# 4.152.0, with the site root as the assets directory): it would upload the
# repository's history from .git (or fail the deploy on a pack over 25 MiB),
# and wrangler's own scratch state in .wrangler is written into the directory
# it runs from, which here IS the assets directory.
.git
.wrangler
wrangler.toml
